course: dictionary
lesson: 7538
title: Precipitation in the water cycle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Precipitation is a long word for water that falls from the sky. It means any water that falls from clouds to the ground, as rain, snow, sleet or hail. «Rain, snow, sleet and hail are all called precipitation.» Each one is a different form of the same thing.
explain: Water does not fall from clouds by accident. Water rises into the air, cools and forms clouds. «When the droplets join together and grow heavy, they fall as rain, snow or hail: this is called precipitation.» The droplets become too heavy to float, so gravity pulls them down.
explain: Precipitation can also mean how much water falls in a place over time. A forecast may say there is a 70 percent chance of precipitation, and a rain gauge measures rainfall in millimetres. Use the context: if the sentence talks about a chance or an amount, it means this second sense.
fact: Precipitation means water that falls from clouds to the ground in any form.
fact: The main forms of precipitation are rain, snow, sleet and hail.
fact: Precipitation is the third stage of the water cycle: evaporation, condensation, precipitation, then collection in rivers, lakes and seas.
fact: The total precipitation in a place over a year is called annual precipitation, and rain gauges measure rainfall in millimetres.
fact: In chemistry, precipitation can also mean a solid forming in a liquid and separating out.
exercise: «Rain, snow, sleet and hail are all called precipitation.» What is precipitation? | *Water that falls from clouds to the ground in any form | Dark grey clouds that gather before a storm | Mist that rises from the ground | Wind that blows across the land
exercise: In the water cycle, which stage comes straight after condensation, when clouds form? | Freezing | *Precipitation | Evaporation | Collection in rivers and seas
exercise: A forecast says there is a 30 percent chance of precipitation. What does this tell you? | The sun will shine for 30 minutes | *There is a chance that rain, snow, sleet or hail will fall | The wind will blow at 30 miles an hour | The temperature will drop by 30 degrees
test: «The rain gauge showed 12 millimetres of precipitation in one day.» What does precipitation mean here? | The speed of the wind | *The amount of rain that fell | The shape of the clouds
test: Which of these is NOT a form of precipitation? | Snow | Sleet | Hail | *Fog
exam: Why do water droplets fall as precipitation? | They freeze in the sea | *They grow heavy, and gravity pulls them down | The sun pushes them back up into the sky | They turn into clouds again straight away
